ion":"SABCO\n\nTHE FOLLOWING MESSAGE IS TRANSMITTED AT THE REQUEST OF THE\nCOLORADO AVALANCHE INFORMATION CENTER.\n\n...A SPECIAL AVALANCHE ADVISORY IN EFFECT FROM 4:30 PM SUNDAY\nUNTIL 4:30 PM MONDAY...\n\n*WHAT...Avalanche conditions are dangerous above treeline.\n*WHERE...San Juan Mountains\n*WHEN... From 4:30 PM Sunday until 4:30 PM Monday.\n*IMPACTS... Backcountry travelers can easily trigger dangerous avalanches large enough to bury a human.\n*PRECAUTION/PREPAREDNESS ACTIONS... A potent winter storm increases avalanche danger Sunday into Monday. Rain, snow, and wind will cause natural avalanches above treeline. Check the forecast at www.colorado.gov/avalanche.\n\n\n\nBeyer","ends":"2026-11-02T17:00:00-07:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Saguache County West of Continental Divide Below 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.fe76f99d50f1dd3da173a38b1d32a5f96ac5311c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.fe76f99d50f1dd3da173a38b1d32a5f96ac5311c.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued November 1 at 1:50PM MST until November 4 at 5:00AM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall will be possible,\nespecially over the western half of San Luis Valley.\n\n* WHERE...The western half of the San Luis Valley, including\nAntonito, Del Norte, Monte Vista and Alamosa.\n\n* WHEN...From 5 PM MST this afternoon through late Tuesday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Runoff from heavy rain and melting snow over the San Juan\nMountains may cause flooding in the San Luis Valley, especially\nMonday and Tuesday as high flows move out of the mountains and\nthrough the Rio Grande and Conejos River.\n- The greatest risk of flooding will be along the Conejos River and\nthe Rio Grande, including Del Norte, Monte Vista and Alamosa.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-11-04T05:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Del Norte Vicinity/Northern San Luis Valley Below 8500 Ft; Alamosa  Vicinity/Central San Luis Valley Below 8500 Ft; Southern San Luis Valley","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6452f67ccada8c80a213b32735fb106e5b65d3ae.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6452f67ccada8c80a213b32735fb106e5b65d3ae.002.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-01T23:52:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 012352 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 452 PM MST Sun Nov 1 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Heavy rainfall will continue across the ern San Juans into the evening, with significant and dangerous flooding expected from the mountains downstream into the western edge of the San Luis Valley. - Snow level finally drops late tonight, with several inches of snow","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-01T23:56:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 012356 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 456 PM MST Sun Nov 1 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-021400- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Feet- Central Chaffee County Below 9000 Feet- Western Mosqu","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=HWO&format=CI"},"fwf":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-02T01:43:00+00:00","snippet":".Discussion... Critical fire weather conditions are not expected over the next 7 days. Heavy rainfall will continue over the San Juan tonight, with rain changing to heavy snow early Monday morning as snow levels fall. The San Juan Range and the San Luis Valley will be at an elevated risk for flooding the next few days, especially from this afternoon into Monday, due to heavy rainfall and po